hypotheses.statement:
Assume the prices satisfy <a href="#eq:dual-test" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:dual-test">[eq:dual-test]</a>, and fix a level $b$. Let $S,D\subseteq V(H_b)$, where $S\cup D$ is contained in a ball of radius $R_0$ in $H$ and meets every part of $\mathcal D$ in at most $P_0$ vertices. Suppose that $$32\le h\le20\ell_0^2,\qquad q(S),q(D)\le e^h,
 \qquad 0\le\eta\le2,$$ and that $\alpha_i,\beta_i\le\eta$ for $i\in S$. If $A$ in <a href="#eq:adjustment-parameters" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:adjustment-parameters">[eq:adjustment-parameters]</a> is sufficiently large depending only on $r$, then $$\label{eq:local-cross}
 e_{q,H_b}(S,D)\le C_1\bigl(\eta hq(S)+e^{-3h}\bigr),$$ where $C_1=C_1(r)$.

For all sufficiently large $\Delta$ depending only on $r$, suppose that a proper partial correspondence coloring and entry weights satisfy availability, <a href="#eq:weight-bounds" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:weight-bounds">[eq:weight-bounds]</a>, and $$\label{eq:mass-window}
 K/2\le W_v\le2K\qquad(v\in V(G')).$$ There is an extension of the partial coloring and a choice of weights on the remaining entries that preserve availability and <a href="#eq:weight-bounds" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:weight-bounds">[eq:weight-bounds]</a>, and satisfy $$\label{eq:round-conclusions}
 W_v^{\mathrm{new}}\le W_v+\xi,\qquad
 F_v^{\mathrm{new}}\le F_v+\xi,\qquad
 \frac{\deg_{\mathrm{new}}(v)}{\Delta}
 \le(1-\tau)\frac{\deg_{G'}(v)}{\Delta}+\xi$$ for every vertex $v$ that remains uncolored.

For the random update just defined, $$\label{eq:round-expectations}
 \begin{aligned}
 \mathbb E\bar W_v&\le W_v+o(\xi),\\
 \mathbb E\bar F_v&\le F_v+\tau(B+1)D_v+o(\xi),\\
 \mathbb E\bar D_{vu}&\ge\tfrac12D_{vu}\qquad(vu\in E(G')).
 \end{aligned}$$

Let $\mathcal E_v$ be the set of edges of $H$ with an endpoint hosted at a neighbor of $v$ in $G'$, and let $X_v$ count the edges of $\mathcal E_v$ whose two endpoints activate. Then $$\label{eq:collision-tail}
 \mathbb P\bigl(4K\Delta^{-0.99}X_v>\zeta\bigr)
 \le O(\Delta^3)e^{e-1-\Delta^{0.01}}+e^{-\Delta^{0.8}}.$$ For either coefficient family in <a href="#eq:neighbor-coefficients" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:neighbor-coefficients">[eq:neighbor-coefficients]</a>, the sum of $b_u$ over hosts $u$ counted by $A_u$ that receive no color is at most $4K\Delta^{-0.99}X_v$.

